  "steps": [
    "Heat the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat and sear the sliced andouille until nicely browned. Remove to a plate.",
    "Add the hot Italian sausage, let it develop a crust, then break it up and cook through. Remove it to the plate.",
    "Add the onion with salt and pepper and saute a few minutes, scraping up the browned bits from the bottom.",
    "Stir in the garlic and sun-dried tomatoes and cook until just fragrant.",
    "Add the tomato paste and cook until deep red, then stir in the basil, oregano, red pepper flakes and bouillon paste and toast for 30 seconds.",
    "Sprinkle in the flour and cook for about 2 minutes, stirring.",
    "Pour in the chicken broth, return both sausages to the pot, and simmer for 10 minutes.",
    "Lower the heat and stir in the cream and parmesan.",
    "Add the tortellini and cook according to the package directions.",
    "Fold in the spinach until just wilted, then taste and adjust the salt.",
    "Stir in the cold butter cubes and serve topped with more parmesan and crisped sausage or tortellini."
  ],
  "equipment": [
    "Dutch oven"
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Brown the two sausages separately so each gets a good crust.",
    "Add the tortellini last so it doesn't overcook."
  ],
